**Read:** [Inorganic Chemical Technology — Nanda Kishore, NPTEL](../sources/Inorganic-Chemical-Technology-Kishore.lingua#r_77Z8T5RFYFNNXZ7XKZFKPRKDKR), all hydrogen/industrial-gas production teaching; [Industrial Chemical Technology II — Nduka, NOUN](../sources/Industrial-Chemical-Technology-II-NOUN.lingua#r_7RXE2GF1DW7QH9GHTCGT0P09SR), the whole hydrogen, water-gas and synthesis-gas units; [Haber–Bosch ammonia in an energy landscape — Smith, Hill and Torrente-Murciano](../sources/Haber-Bosch-Ammonia-Smith-Hill-Torrente.lingua#r_6CX46VQ3D3W0W059Y55D44MMAQ), the complete hydrogen-production, separation and system-boundary analysis; [Chemical Reactor Analysis and Design Fundamentals — Rawlings and Ekerdt](../sources/Chemical-Reactor-Analysis-Rawlings-Ekerdt.lingua#r_7YQAV27Y3J0B537Z6K5HDN8H0A), the full relevant thermodynamic/energy and reaction-balance reasoning.

Hydrogen can be produced from water, hydrocarbons, biomass-derived feeds and other chemical systems. The molecule does not encode its production route. Compare the actual feed, chemical reactions, energy carriers, co-products, purification and delivery state, preserving upstream assumptions and measured evidence.

For water electrolysis, 2H₂O→2H₂+O₂ gives a stoichiometric and charge basis. Reversible work, thermoneutral heat and measured cell/system input are different quantities. For hydrocarbon-derived hydrogen, reforming, shift, heat supply and separation connect carbon and hydrogen accounts; reporting reactor conversion alone omits consequential duties.

The required product may need removal of water, carbon compounds, sulfur species, oxygen or other constituents. Compression, storage, contact materials, leakage and continuity of supply affect usable hydrogen. A general energy label cannot establish catalyst compatibility or a complete process comparison.

**Work:** reconstruct two complete hydrogen routes feeding the same downstream chemical process. Independently close stoichiometric, energy and consequential contaminant accounts at a defined delivery pressure/quality and time basis. Compare observed, modeled and projected performance and quantify which uncertainty could change the preferred route.

**Continue:** [Explain synthesis gas through feed chemistry, reaction paths and product requirements](Synthesis-gas-reforming-gasification-and-composition.lingua#r_54CH7SW9WFFBJ00FMN2BVRTCMQ).

